sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) PRL / Gerbode et al. (2012) Science Kirchhoff elastic rod tendril perversion, G-fiber overwinding & Pass 3 thigmotropic contact coiling — MorphoEval overall 91.7/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py` (overall weighted score ~91.7/100, down from 93.1 in v2). The single v2 remediation item is closed in reduced form: a new implicit overdamped discrete-rod section 3b simulates contact-gated thigmotropic coiling around a rigid cylindrical support with Coulomb support friction and self-contact friction, producing N_wrap = 2.86 turns after 30 min (no-support control 0.31, kappa0 stays 0), first full wrap at 4.75 min, max support penetration < 0.025 mm, max axial strain < 2 %, F_hold(mu) = {0.0005, 0.108, 0.212, 0.27} mN monotone in mu with the frictionless coil slipping at the first load increment, 11 active self-contact pairs with min non-adjacent distance / 2a = 0.989 in the stacked-turns scenario, and wraps(R_s = 2) / wraps(R_s = 1) = 0.64. The Pass 2 results are unchanged (pitchfork r = 0.9974, |Delta_Lk| = 0, soft overwinding r = 0.9806, 4-species r = 0.9999, specimen CV = 0.298). The score goes down because re-verification shows the v2 audit misquoted two measurements (Gerbode peak overwinding 0.7171 vs ref 0.58 and kappa_0 0.4976 vs ref 0.65 mm^-1, not 0.5873 and 0.6545), and because the six new measurements are internal controls or scheme-consistency checks rather than comparisons with measured contact-coiling data. Overall 91.7/100 (faithfulness 90.7, reproducibility 94.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8a7928d7; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 94, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 94, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature_comparison.png: rendered output of 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py at 8a7928d7, image/png, 1061305 B, 2757×1458 px, artifact_sha256 57eed032cffcc9361a1a8fa3afc14d6c5377dfa2d824686d569b7ebc68f50f73 (sha256 57eed032cffcc9361a1a8fa3afc14d6c5377dfa2d824686d569b7ebc68f50f73), spec_fingerprint 68cb059282e6586e1c698e0a2073f9ca8cb2a88dda3dd3ce0c564cd556b97a7e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 68cb059282e6586e1c698e0a2073f9ca8cb2a88dda3dd3ce0c564cd556b97a7e; artifact_sha256: 57eed032cffcc9361a1a8fa3afc14d6c5377dfa2d824686d569b7ebc68f50f73; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/paper_citations.bib=2529ebe7e9abea2f..., datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/scout_manifest.json=801e196968b34405..., datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/tendril_perversion_helix_specimen.jpg=14409d193142442d..., datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature_reference.json=8af7ac3175f6890f..., datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/thigmotropic_contact_coiling_reference.json=f55d9cfe319f0366...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Goriely & Tabor (1998) / McMillen & Goriely (2002): an intrinsically curved Kirchhoff rod with both ends held undergoes a supercritical pitchfork bifurcation below T_c = B kappa_0^2 / (1 + Gamma) into two opposite-handed helices joined by a perversion, with zero net link | Gerbode et al. (2012): the cucumber tendril's G-fiber ribbon sets the intrinsic curvature; soft tendrils (Gamma < 1) overwind under axial stretch while lignified ones unwind; coil radius and pitch scale across species | Darwin (1865) Ch. IV: tendrils curve toward a touched side within tens of seconds, complete a wrap around a thin stick within minutes to about an hour, and grasp thin supports more readily than thick ones (qualitative) | Jaffe & Galston (1968): thigmotropic coiling is a contact-triggered, propagating growth response; Euler (1762): the capstan law exp(mu Theta) for a flexible line on a cylinder; reconstructed_in_script: Timoshenko bilayer kappa_0, exact T_c, 161-node L-BFGS-B Kirchhoff perversion solver with zero-link enforcement and negative controls; 10-point pitchfork sweep; soft vs lignified overwinding; 4-species scaling; DoG segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Passiflora caerulea specimen (Pass 2) | Pass 3: 61-node inertia-free discrete rod with contact-gated intrinsic curvature pointing toward the support axis, implicit backward-Euler incremental potential (L-BFGS-B), rigid-cylinder penalty contact, penalty self-contact, lagged-normal Coulomb friction on support and self-contact, quasi-static grip test vs mu*sum(N) and exp(mu Theta); no-support, frictionless, friction-sweep, support-radius-sweep and stacked-turns scenarios; transfer_boundary: The contact solver is a separate bending-only rod: it has no material-frame twist, so Gamma = C/B plays no role in contact coiling and the perversion (zero-link) physics of section 3 is not coupled to it | mu_support, mu_self, kappa_contact, tau_thigmo, v_signal, the 55 deg approach angle and the initial placement touching the support at 25 % of L are provenance-tagged assumptions; the only empirical anchors for Pass 3 are Darwin's qualitative timings and support-size statements | Friction uses normal forces lagged one macro step; F_hold / mu*sum(N) = 0.67 is a consistency check of the scheme, not an experiment; N_wrap counts loose loops that enclose but do not touch the support (contact fraction 33 % of nodes); does_not_claim: Circumnutation or support-search before first touch, a measured tendril-on-wood friction coefficient, compliant or rough or finite-length supports, G-fiber lignification time course, or a validated time-to-wrap (tau_thigmo and v_signal were chosen inside Darwin's 5-60 min window and the model's 4.75 min falls slightly below it)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:1221, 897-899 and 2051-2056 — housekeeping: the section-6 banner still says '6-Panel'; `_last_objective`, `_mat_dir`, `_last_opt_message` are unused and `last_objective` is unbound when t_end_min < dt_min; the determinism check covers only a 5 min horizon. Also morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_064_tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature.lean:1-12 — the header lists only the three Pass 2 sources although Laws 4-5 cite Darwin (1865), Jaffe & Galston (1968) and Euler (1762).",
            "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:1841-1850 and 1831-1840 — the time-to-first-wrap measurement (4.75 min vs reference 32.5 min) is set by the assumed tau_thigmo = 5 min and v_signal = 5 mm/min and falls below Darwin's 5-60 min window, and N_wrap uses the no-support control as its reference. Pass 4: either digitise a quantitative time course (e.g. Jaffe & Galston 1968 Fig. or Isnard & Silk 2009 Table) into the JSON and fit tau_thigmo/v_signal to it, or move both entries out of `measure_morphoeval()` into a 'predictions' list so the quick gate does not count them as reference-anchored.",
            "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:1925-1933 and 1955-1963 — the Gerbode soft peak overwinding (0.7171 vs 0.58 turns, +24 %) and the G-fiber bilayer kappa_0 (0.4976 vs 0.65 mm^-1, -23 %) miss their references by about a quarter; v2 misquoted both. Pass 4: revisit `compute_g_fiber_intrinsic_curvature` (L164-L181) bilayer thickness/modulus ratio against Gerbode et al. (2012) Fig. 2 and the overwinding amplitude in `evaluate_gerbode_overwinding_regimes` (L1040-L1088), and report the deviations in the figure.",
            "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:483-514 and 1588-1591 — `_wrap_statistics` counts winding of every distal node about the support axis, so N_wrap = 2.86 with only 33 % of nodes in contact includes loose loops (mean loop radius > R_s + a), yet panel G's title reports \"N = 2.9\" without the qualifier. Pass 4: report tight wraps (nodes with rho < R_s + a + tol) separately from enclosing loops, add a contact-feedback growth law so kappa0 keeps rising until contact (the JSON `residual_remediation` already proposes this), and label panel G accordingly.",
            "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:596-909 vs 249-411 — the contact-coiling rod is a separate bending-only discrete rod with no material-frame twist, so Gamma = C/B (the quantity that drives Laws 2-3) plays no role in contact coiling and the zero-link perversion physics is never solved together with support contact. Pass 4: add a twist degree of freedom (Cosserat / Bishop-frame twist angle per edge) to the section 3b rod, or drive section 3 `relax_kirchhoff_perversion_rod` with the contact-gated kappa0 and a cylinder constraint, and show that a tethered tendril wrapping a support still forms a perversion.",
            "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:741-761 and 1851-1860 — Coulomb friction uses normal forces lagged one macro step, so F_hold / mu*sum(N) = 0.67 is partly a numerical artefact of the lag plus partial contact; the self-test accepts any value in (0.1, 1.5) (L2044). Pass 4: iterate the normal force to self-consistency within each macro step (or use a semi-smooth Newton / augmented-Lagrangian contact step), then tighten the acceptance band and report the capstan-law comparison exp(mu Theta) as a measurement.",
            "remediation needed: morphoeval/cloud/dispatches/slot-064.json `slug` (\"human-brain-folding-3d\") and the pass3 run yaml `paper` field (Tallinen et al. 2016) do not describe this tendril script; both are campaign metadata outside this slot's writable files (`init` sets the run paper). Flagged for the campaign coordinator rather than edited." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.917"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 064 Pass 3 Phase B Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

